PATCH 492: the WAYPOINT-REACHED dispatcher ac0a and its four handlers -- one base-loss that crashed the
self-play of at least six missions at an identical stack.

asm 0x1ac0a-0x1ac30 (DS=DGROUP=0x1c00, CS=0x0f69), reached from ad11 when an object comes within 0x30 of
its current waypoint: si = its waypoint list word[DGROUP:0x7d2a + byte[di+0x1b]*2] (the same goal-group
table the objective scan 6507 walks), bx = the mission waypoint MODE word[DGROUP:(word[DGROUP:0x9796]+2)]
clamped to 0..3, then `call word[CS:0xb5a1 + bx*2]` -- CS is the 0x0f69 cluster, so the targets are linear
0x1ac39/0x1ac5d/0x1ac81/0x1aca5.  Ghidra read word[0x9796] as a HOST pointer and dereferenced `+2` through
it (SIGSEGV), mis-based the CS table to segment 0x1000 and dropped DI.  The four targets are mid-block
entries Ghidra never made functions: three CONSUME the reached waypoint (decrement byte[si], shift the
8-byte entries down from si+0x14 to si+0xc) and the fourth ROTATES the list (saving the first entry and
writing it back into the last slot -- a patrol loop); they are added here together with their icall-map
entries.  A 47-mission native crash sweep found AZER4, AZER6, CYPRUS5, CYPRUS6, SAUDI1 and INDIA5 all
SEGV'ing at exactly ac0a <- ad11 <- ad08 <- ab03.
